{"name":"A Month of Sundays","hex":"#b0b2bc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"month","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period into which a year is divided, historically based on the phases of the moon.","A period of 30 days, 31 days, or some alternation thereof."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/month"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Month of Sundays (2015 film)","blocks":[{"text":"A Month of Sundays is a 2015 Australian film starring Anthony LaPaglia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Month_of_Sundays_(2015_film)"},{"title":"Month","blocks":[{"text":"A month is a unit of time, used with calendars, that is approximately as long as a natural phase cycle of the Moon; the words month and Moon are cognates. The traditional concept of months arose with the cycle of Moon phases; such lunar months (\"lunations\") are synodic months and last approximately 29.53 days, making for roughly 12.37 such months in one Earth year. From excavated tally sticks, researchers have deduced that people counted days in relation to the Moon's phases as early as the Paleolithic age. Synodic months, based on the Moon's orbital period with respect to the Earth–Sun line, are still the basis of many calendars today and are used to divide the year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg/330px-2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Month"},{"title":"The Sundays","blocks":[{"text":"The Sundays were an English alternative rock band formed in Bristol in 1988. The band's lineup consisted of lead vocalist Harriet Wheeler, guitarist David Gavurin, bassist Paul Brindley, and drummer Patrick Hannan. Their music combined jangling guitar arrangements with Wheeler's distinctive vocals, drawing on elements of dream pop and indie pop."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/The_Sundays.gif/330px-The_Sundays.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sundays"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f6/Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg/250px-Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f6/Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg/250px-Amonthofsundays2015poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmonthofsundays2015poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg/500px-2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg/1280px-2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg/500px-2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Among its many features, the Prague astronomical clock has medallions to represent the months ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2015_Zegar_astronomiczny_w_Pradze_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/The_Sundays.gif/330px-The_Sundays.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig